alue": "It was like following him, so to speak, like that. And uh, Nat Hentoff had written sort of a memoir or memories of Duke in, I think it was Village Voice, and uh, when I read that and it.... You know, sometimes the little things have to be triggers and he was talking about how Duke was, how proud Duke was of being a black American, and his music [was] based on his race, a lot of \"em, you know: \"...", "type": "string"}, "datatype": "string"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q18619$B48798DC-7BA3-4C9A-82E2-7D895A90B10D", "rank": "normal"}]}}